==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[carrom]]

===Etymology===
Probably corrupted from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|carambole}} (the red ball in [[billiards]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ˈkærʌm|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ærʌm|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|cue sports|especially billiards}} A [[shot]] in which the [[ball]] [[struck]] with the [[cue]] comes in contact with two or more [[balls]] on the [[table]]; a hitting of two or more balls with the player's ball.
# A billiard-like [[India]]n game in which players take turns flicking checker-like pieces into one of four goals on the corners of (one meter by one meter square) board.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|shot in which the cue ball strikes two balls}} [[cannon]] {{qualifier|UK}}

